# Xavier Mesh License v1.0

## Preamble
Xavier is an open-source cognitive memory system licensed under MIT for standalone use.
This Mesh License applies when you activate Xavier's peer-to-peer, governance, or Data Commons features.

## Acceptance
By enabling any feature behind the `mesh` feature gate (`--features mesh` or `mesh.enabled = true` in config),
you agree to the following terms:

## Terms

### 1. Network Participation
- Your node becomes part of the Xavier Mesh network
- Node identity is derived from an Ed25519 keypair
- You may opt in or out of Data Commons telemetry at any time
- Data Commons data is anonymized by default

### 2. Governance Rights
- Active nodes earn voting rights proportional to XP + reputation + activity
- Voting is anonymous, non-delegable, and requires activity in the last 7 days
- The Xavier Core Council retains veto power over security-critical proposals (66% vote)

### 3. XP Tokenomics
- XP tokens are earned through contribution to the mesh (telemetry, validation, sync)
- XP can be staked, spent, or transferred
- XP has no monetary value and is non-redeemable for fiat currency

### 4. Data Sovereignty
- Your data never leaves your node encrypted at rest
- Data Commons sharing is opt-in with granular consent levels (None/Metadata/Anonymized/Full)
- You may revoke consent at any time

### 5. Termination
- You may exit the mesh at any time by disabling mesh features
- XP balance is preserved locally but becomes non-transferable
- Governance rights cease upon exit

### 6. No Warranty
This software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied.
